theorem set-image
  let Y be a set                                                      (H1)
  let Z be a set                                                      (H2)
  let E : Y → Z                                                       (H3)
  let u be an element                                                 (H4)
  assume u ∈ {E(s) : s ∈ Y}                                           (H5)
  then there is s ∈ Y with u = E(s)

1.  There is s ∈ Y with u = E(s).
    def:stdlib/functions/set-image, from H5
